    "status": "present",
    "value": "For stones on distinct integer coordinates, return minimum and maximum endpoint moves until consecutive, moving an endpoint only to a non-endpoint vacant position. The approach is: sliding length-n window minimizes moves, with endpoint-only special case; extrema bound maximum. Its target cost is O(n log n) time/O(n) space. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
